    detailedAnswer: 'You could save everything into a text file. It works for ten users and falls apart after that. Finding one user means reading the entire file. Two people saving at the same moment can corrupt it. A crash halfway through a save leaves it broken. A database solves exactly these: indexes so it can find one row without reading everything, locking so simultaneous writes do not clash, and transactions so a half-finished change is undone rather than left broken.',
