    shortAnswerHi: 'Create, Read, Update, Delete — data ke saath hone wale chaar kaam. SQL mein: INSERT, SELECT, UPDATE, DELETE.',
    detailedAnswer: 'Almost every app is these four operations over and over. Add a user, show the users, change a user, remove a user. Once you see it, most backend work is recognisably CRUD with rules layered on top. In SQL they are INSERT, SELECT, UPDATE, DELETE. Over HTTP they are POST, GET, PUT/PATCH, DELETE. Two of them are dangerous: UPDATE and DELETE without a WHERE clause will change or erase every row in the table. Run the SELECT with the same WHERE first, see what comes back, then run the real one.',
