    shortAnswer: 'GET asks for something and changes nothing. POST sends data to create or change something.',
    shortAnswerHi: 'GET kuch maangta hai aur kuch badalta nahi. POST data bhejta hai kuch banane ya badalne ke liye.',
    detailedAnswer: 'GET is reading: opening a page, fetching a list. It should never change anything on the server, which is why refreshing a GET is always safe and browsers may cache it. Its data rides in the URL, so it is visible in history and server logs — never put a password there. POST is writing: submitting a form, creating an order. Its data goes in the body, not the URL. And POST is not safe to repeat — that is exactly why browsers warn you before resubmitting a form, and why pressing "Pay" twice can charge you twice.',
    detailedAnswerHi: 'GET padhna hai: page kholna, list laana. Ise server par kuch badalna nahi chahiye, isiliye GET refresh karna hamesha safe hai aur browsers use cache kar sakte hain. Iska data URL mein jata hai, isliye history aur server logs mein dikhta hai — password wahan kabhi mat daalo. POST likhna hai: form bhejna, order banana. Iska data body mein jata hai, URL mein nahi. Aur POST dohraana safe nahi hai — isiliye browser form dobara bhejne se pehle warning deta hai, aur "Pay" do baar dabane se do baar paise kat sakte hain.',
