    detailedAnswer: 'The first digit tells you almost everything. 2xx means success — 200 is a normal OK, 201 means something was created. 4xx means the request was wrong: 400 the server could not understand it, 401 you are not logged in, 403 you are logged in but not allowed, 404 no such thing exists. 5xx means the server broke while handling a perfectly valid request — that is a bug on the backend, not the caller\'s fault. The 401-versus-403 distinction gets asked constantly: 401 is "who are you?", 403 is "I know who you are, and no".',
    detailedAnswerHi: 'Pehla digit lagbhag sab bata deta hai. 2xx matlab success — 200 normal OK, 201 matlab kuch bana. 4xx matlab request galat thi: 400 server samajh nahi paya, 401 aap logged in nahi ho, 403 logged in ho par ijazat nahi, 404 aisi cheez hai hi nahi. 5xx matlab bilkul sahi request handle karte hue server toot gaya — ye backend ka bug hai, bhejne wale ki galti nahi. 401 vs 403 baar-baar poocha jata hai: 401 "aap kaun ho?", 403 "pata hai aap kaun ho, aur nahi".',
