    question: 'What is Git, and how is GitHub different?',
    shortAnswer: 'Git saves versions of your work on your computer. GitHub is a website that hosts those saved versions online.',
    shortAnswerHi: 'Git aapke computer par kaam ke versions save karta hai. GitHub ek website hai jo un versions ko online rakhti hai.',
    detailedAnswer: 'Git is the tool. It remembers every version of your project, so you can see what changed, who changed it, and go back if something breaks — no more "final_v2_FINAL_really.zip". It works completely offline, on your own machine. GitHub is a website that stores a copy of your Git history online, so others can see it and collaborate. Git works fine without GitHub; GitHub is meaningless without Git. Alternatives like GitLab and Bitbucket do the same job.',
    detailedAnswerHi: 'Git ek tool hai. Wo aapke project ka har version yaad rakhta hai, taaki aap dekh sako kya badla, kisne badla, aur kuch toot jaye to wapas ja sako — ab "final_v2_FINAL_really.zip" ki zarurat nahi. Ye poori tarah offline, aapki apni machine par chalta hai. GitHub ek website hai jo aapki Git history ki copy online rakhti hai, taaki doosre dekh sakein aur saath kaam kar sakein. Git GitHub ke bina bhi chalta hai; GitHub Git ke bina bekaar hai. GitLab aur Bitbucket wahi kaam karte hain.',
