    detailedAnswer: 'These four cover almost everything you do daily. git add is packing a box — you choose which changed files go in. git commit seals the box with a label describing what changed; it is now saved on your computer, permanently, and you can always come back to it. git push sends your sealed boxes to GitHub so others can see them. git pull brings down boxes other people pushed. The most common beginner surprise is that commit does not upload anything — it is local until you push.',
    detailedAnswerHi: 'Ye chaar lagbhag rozana ka poora kaam hain. git add dabba pack karna hai — aap chunte ho kaun si badli hui files jayengi. git commit dabbe ko seal karke label lagata hai jisme likha hai kya badla; ab wo aapke computer par pakka save hai aur aap kabhi bhi wapas aa sakte ho. git push aapke seal kiye dabbe GitHub par bhejta hai taaki doosre dekh sakein. git pull wo dabbe le aata hai jo doosron ne push kiye. Beginners ko sabse zyada ye chaunkata hai ki commit kuch upload nahi karta — push tak wo sirf local hota hai.',
