    detailedAnswer: 'Your main branch should always work. If you build a new feature directly on it and get halfway, main is now broken — and if you need to fix an urgent bug, there is nowhere clean to do it from. A branch is your own copy: experiment freely, and if it goes wrong, delete the branch and nothing is lost. When it works, merge it back into main. This is also how teams avoid stepping on each other — everyone works on their own branch and merges when ready.',
