    question: 'What is a merge conflict and how do you fix it?',
    shortAnswer: 'Two people changed the same lines, so Git cannot decide which to keep. You choose, remove the markers, and commit.',
    shortAnswerHi: 'Do logon ne wahi lines badli, isliye Git tay nahi kar pata kaun si rakhe. Aap chunte ho, markers hataate ho, aur commit karte ho.',
    detailedAnswer: 'Git merges automatically when changes touch different places. When two people edited the same lines, it refuses to guess and marks the spot with <<<<<<< and >>>>>>> showing both versions. Nothing is broken and nothing is lost — Git is asking a question. Open the file, decide what the final code should be (sometimes one side, sometimes a combination), delete the marker lines, then add and commit. The fear beginners have is that a conflict means damage; it does not. It means Git was careful enough not to choose for you.',
